#################################################################
### Building of the design for Geri:
#################################################################


git submodule update --init
cd buildsystem

# Make sure that Vivado 2021.2 is visible in the system path
# If you tries to build for some other Vivado version before
./make_project.sh

# Warning!!!!
# The script build may fail on building the block desing with following error:

# generate_target all [get_ips]
ERROR: [Vivado 12-3563] The Nested sub-design '/home/gumas/projects/cbm/geri_fresh/hdl/pcie_wrapper/versatile_dma/dma_mover2/hdl/src/bd/ip/design_1_axi4s_src3_0_0/design_1_axi4s_src3_0_0.xci' can only be generated by its parent sub-design.
INFO: [Common 17-206] Exiting Vivado at Thu Oct 21 15:42:18 2021...
Makefile:9: recipe for target 'geri_versions_0.xpr' failed
make: *** [geri_versions_0.xpr] Error 1


One must open the project with Vivado GUI (build/geri_versions_0/example-vivado/geri_versions_0.xpr) and run the implementation. It should succeed.

#################################################################
### Preparing for run
#################################################################

Use buildsystem/make_artifacts.sh to backup bitstream and agwb artifacts.
After configuring some paths in make_artifacts one may run:
./make_artifacts.sh -etrl
to create artifacts and send them to remote host (probably after some configurations of paths inside the script).


On remote PC unpack the artifacts and copy agwb definions to soft directory.
Geri agwb definions should be located in soft/agwb/agwb
GBTxEMU AGWB definions should be located in soft/agwb_emu/agwb_emu.
On JINR PC there is /home/geri/mg/select_artifacts.sh that simplifies that.

Source soft/add_python_paths.sh to add all python modules to path.

################################################################# 
## FPGA driver
#################################################################

After configuring the FPGA one must reboot the PC
After reboot one must:

modprobe uio_pci_generic 
echo "32ab 7025" > /sys/bus/pci/drivers/uio_pci_generic/new_id

################################################################# 
## Example test
#################################################################

# on work host:
./make_project.sh
## open vivado project
## write bitstream

./make_artifacts.sh -etrl

# on test host
## run hw_server
## configure FPGA
reboot

cd mg
./select_artifacts.sh ../artifacts/master_88_78191393_geri_example.tgz
sudo su
. ./c1.sh
ipython3 -i gbt_access.py